description:
Write `newEmitter()` returning an object with:

- `on(name, fn)`: adds a listener and returns a function that removes exactly that listener;
- `once(name, fn)`: a listener that removes itself after its first call;
- `off(name)`: removes every listener for `name`;
- `emit(name, ...)`: calls the listeners for `name` in the order they were added, with the extra arguments, and returns how many were called.

A listener that adds or removes listeners while `emit` is running must not upset that `emit`: it calls exactly the listeners that were there when it started (minus any `once` listener that already ran).

starter.solution.lua:
function newEmitter()
    local listeners = {}
    local e = {}
    function e.on(name, fn)
        listeners[name] = fn
    end
    function e.emit(name, ...)
        if listeners[name] then listeners[name](...) end
        return 0
    end
    return e
end
